        "original_id": "6f4ba99c-bd84-5dee-9bdc-21cdda01b70a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William McKinley\n- Laws: McKinley Tariff, Tariff Act of 1890\n- Organizations: United States Congress, Republican Party\n- Events: United States elections of 1890, Panic of 1890\n- Roles: President of the United States, Representative\n\nFacts:\n- William McKinley framed the Tariff Act of 1890 as a Representative in the United States Congress.\n- The Tariff Act of 1890, commonly called the McKinley Tariff, became law on October 1, 1890.\n- In the United States elections of 1890, the Republicans suffered major losses because of the Panic of 1890 and the unpopularity of the McKinley Tariff.\n- William McKinley was the 25th President of the United States from March 4, 1897 until his assassination in September 1901, six months into his second term.",
